# ============================================================================
# LOGS & CACHE
# ============================================================================
logs/
*.log
data/cache/
data/backtest_results/
# src/dashboard/build_dashboard.py output -- uploaded straight to GitHub Pages by the
# workflows as a build artifact, never committed to the repo
public/
# runtime risk state (halt/daily-loss/EOD dedup) and CSVs (order history) are ignored by
# default... EXCEPT the specific runtime files negated below: GitHub Actions runners are
# ephemeral (a fresh checkout every scheduled run), so those have to be committed back to the
# repo by the workflow itself or trade history / the kill-switch state would silently reset
# every run. NOTE: a `#` anywhere but the start of a .gitignore line is NOT a comment -- it's
# read as a literal part of the pattern, silently matching nothing. Keep comments on their own
# line, never trailing a pattern (this exact mistake previously left both lines below inert).
data/risk/*.json
*.csv
!data/orders/trade_log.csv
!data/risk/halt_state.json
!data/risk/daily_loss_state.json
!data/risk/eod_summary_state.json
!data/orders/.gitkeep
!data/backtest_results/.gitkeep
!data/cache/.gitkeep
!data/risk/.gitkeep

# ============================================================================
